#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-http-push(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:7
msgid "git-http-push - Push objects over HTTP/DAV to another repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:13
msgid ""
"'git http-push' [--all] [--dry-run] [--force] [--verbose] <URL> <ref> "
"[<ref>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:18
msgid ""
"Sends missing objects to the remote repository, and updates the remote "
"branch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:22
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*NOTE*: This command is temporarily disabled if your libcurl\n"
"is older than 7.16, as the combination has been reported\n"
"not to work and sometimes corrupts the repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--all::`\n"
"\tDo not assume that the remote repository is complete in its\n"
"\tcurrent state, and verify all objects in the entire local\n"
"\tref's history exist in the remote repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--force::`\n"
"\tUsually, the command refuses to update a remote ref that\n"
"\tis not an ancestor of the local ref used to overwrite it.\n"
"\tThis flag disables the check.  What this means is that\n"
"\tthe remote repository can lose commits; use it with\n"
"\tcare.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--dry-run::`\n"
"\tDo everything except actually send the updates.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--verbose::`\n"
"\tReport the list of objects being walked locally and the\n"
"\tlist of objects successfully sent to the remote repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`-d::`\n"
"`-D::`\n"
"\tRemove <ref> from remote repository.  The specified branch\n"
"\tcannot be the remote HEAD.  If -d is specified, the following\n"
"\tother conditions must also be met:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:51
msgid "Remote HEAD must resolve to an object that exists locally"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:52
msgid "Specified branch resolves to an object that exists locally"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:53
msgid "Specified branch is an ancestor of the remote HEAD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "<ref>..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:56
msgid "The remote refs to update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "SPECIFYING THE REFS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:65
msgid ""
"A '<ref>' specification can be either a single pattern, or a pair of such "
"patterns separated by a colon \":\" (this means that a ref name cannot have "
"a colon in it).  A single pattern '<name>' is just a shorthand for "
"'<name>:<name>'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:70
msgid ""
"Each pattern pair '<src>:<dst>' consists of the source side (before the "
"colon) and the destination side (after the colon).  The ref to be pushed is "
"determined by finding a match that matches the source side, and where it is "
"pushed is determined by using the destination side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:73
msgid "It is an error if '<src>' does not match exactly one of the local refs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:75
msgid "If '<dst>' does not match any remote ref, either"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:78
msgid ""
"it has to start with \"refs/\"; <dst> is used as the destination literally "
"in this case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:82
msgid ""
"<src> == <dst> and the ref that matched the <src> must not exist in the set "
"of remote refs; the ref matched <src> locally is used as the name of the "
"destination."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:88
msgid ""
"Without `--force`, the <src> ref is stored at the remote only if <dst> does "
"not exist, or <dst> is a proper subset (i.e. an ancestor) of <src>.  This "
"check, known as \"fast-forward check\", is performed to avoid accidentally "
"overwriting the remote ref and losing other peoples' commits from there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:90
msgid "With `--force`, the fast-forward check is disabled for all refs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-http-push.txt:93
msgid ""
"Optionally, a <ref> parameter can be prefixed with a plus '+' sign to "
"disable the fast-forward check only on that ref."
msgstr ""

